# Copy this file to ".env" and fill it in.
# These values stay server-side (read by the Vite dev middleware in
# server/extractPlugin.js, and by api/extract.js on Vercel). They are NEVER
# exposed to the browser. Do NOT add a VITE_ prefix — that would leak them into
# client code.

# Required: your Anthropic API key.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Optional: a shared passphrase that gates the extraction + sync endpoints.
# Leave it UNSET for open local dev. SET it when you deploy publicly (e.g. on
# Vercel) so only people who know it can spend your API budget / storage. The
# app asks for it once and remembers it on the device.
# APP_PASSPHRASE=choose-a-long-random-phrase

# Optional: cloud sync across devices. Provisioned automatically when you add an
# Upstash Redis store in the Vercel dashboard (Storage tab) — Vercel injects
# these. For LOCAL dev sync, run `vercel env pull .env.local` or paste them here.
# (No VITE_ prefix — they stay server-side.)
# KV_REST_API_URL=https://your-db-xxxxx.upstash.io
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=your-rest-token

# Optional: use Google Maps for EVERYTHING location-related — the trip map, the
# "search & add a place" box, place ratings/hours/website/photos, geocoding, and
# the destination hero photos. Without this key, the app uses free fallbacks
# (OpenStreetMap map, Open-Meteo geocoding, Wikipedia photos) and the add-a-place
# box becomes paste-a-link only — so it always works.
#
# Setup: on ONE Google Cloud key, enable + BILLING on, and restrict the key to
# these APIs and to your domain(s) + http://localhost:5173 (HTTP referrers):
#   - Maps JavaScript API        (the map itself)
#   - Places API (New)           (search/add, details, photos) — the "(New)" one!
#   - Geocoding API              (place names -> coordinates; recommended)
# This is a CLIENT key (the SDK runs in the browser, so the VITE_ prefix is
# intentional and the key ships in the bundle) — the referrer + API restriction
# is what protects it.
#
# Cost (Google's March-2025 per-SKU pricing, billed at the highest field tier a
# call touches): adding a place stays on the cheaper tiers; ratings/hours/photos
# are fetched once per place on demand, then cached + synced so they never
# re-bill. Free monthly allowances (~10K geocoding / 5K Pro / 1K Enterprise) cover
# personal use. Google place photos require visible attribution (the app shows it).
# VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=AIza...
